:HELP NAME=CHGDDMF.Change DDM File (CHGDDMF)
:P.Use the Change DDM File (CHGDDMF) command to change a DDM file.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/FILE'.DDM file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/RMTFILE'.Remote file (RMTFILE)
:P.The remote file for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. File
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Nonstandard file name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/RMTLOCNAME'.Remote location (RMTLOCNAME)
:P.The remote location name of the system at the other end of the
connection.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RDB.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Name or address
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 254 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*SNA:EPK.
:PD.SNA.
:PT.:PK.*IP:EPK.
:PD.TCP/IP.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/LVLCHK'.Record format level check (LVLCHK)
:P.Whether the record format level identifiers of the file are checked
against those the program was compiled with when the file is opened.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.They are not checked.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RMTFILE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/RDB'.Relational database (RDB)
:P.The relational database for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 18 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 1 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. APPC device description
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/LCLLOCNAME'.Local location (LCLLOCNAME)
:P.The local location name this system uses on the connection.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PK.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/MODE'.Mode (MODE)
:P.The mode for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/RMTNETID'.Remote network identifier (RMTNETID)
:P.The network identifier of the remote location.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PK.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/PORT'.Port number (PORT)
:P.The TCP or UDP port number.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*DRDA:EPK.
:PD.DRDA, the distributed relational database protocol.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/ACCMTH'.Access method (ACCMTH)
:P.The access method for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RMTFILE, *COMBINED.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Remote file attribute
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*KEYED:EPK.
:PD.Keyed.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ARRIVAL.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Local access method
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BOTH:EPK.
:PD.Both.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RANDOM, *SEQUENTIAL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGDDMF/PTCCNV'.Protected conversation (PTCCNV)
:P.The protected conversation for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTDDMF.Create DDM File (CRTDDMF)
:P.The Create DDM File (CRTDDMF) command works with a DDM file, a local
name for a file on another system.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/FILE'.DDM file (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/RMTFILE'.Remote file (RMTFILE)
:P.The remote file for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. File
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Nonstandard file name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/RMTLOCNAME'.Remote location (RMTLOCNAME)
