:P.Also accepted&colon. *RDB.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Name or address
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*DEVD:EPK.
:PD.The value of the device description.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 254 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Type
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SNA:EPK.
:PD.SNA.
:PT.:PK.*IP:EPK.
:PD.TCP/IP.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/RDB'.Relational database (RDB)
:P.The relational database for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 18 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/TEXT'.Text (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 1 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. APPC device description
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/LCLLOCNAME'.Local location (LCLLOCNAME)
:P.The local location name this system uses on the connection.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PK.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/MODE'.Mode (MODE)
:P.The mode for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/RMTNETID'.Remote network identifier (RMTNETID)
:P.The network identifier of the remote location.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LOC:EPK.
:PD.The location.
:PT.:PK.*NETATR:EPK.
:PD.The value of the network attributes (DSPNETA).
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/PORT'.Port number (PORT)
:P.The TCP or UDP port number.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DRDA:EPK.
:PD.DRDA, the distributed relational database protocol.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 65535.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/ACCMTH'.Access method (ACCMTH)
:P.The access method for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RMTFILE, *COMBINED.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Remote file attribute
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*KEYED:EPK.
:PD.Keyed.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ARRIVAL.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Local access method
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BOTH:EPK.
:PD.Both.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RANDOM, *SEQUENTIAL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/SHARE'.Share open data path (SHARE)
:P.Whether the open data path of the file is shared with other programs
of the job that open it with SHARE(*YES)&colon. they then share the
file's position and buffers.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The program gets an open data path of its own.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.The open data path is shared.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/PTCCNV'.Protected conversation (PTCCNV)
:P.Whether to protected conversation.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/LVLCHK'.Record format level check (LVLCHK)
:P.Whether the record format level identifiers of the file are checked
against those the program was compiled with when the file is opened.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.They are not checked.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *RMTFILE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTDDMF/REPLACE'.Replace file (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKDDMF.Work with DDM Files (WRKDDMF)
:P.Use the Work with DDM Files (WRKDDMF) command to list DDM files and
where each goes.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKDDMF/FILE'.File (FILE)
:P.The file, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PK.*USRLIBL:EPK.
:PD.The libraries of the user part of the library list.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*ALLUSR:EPK.
:PD.Every user library&colon. libraries whose names do not start with Q,
and the Q libraries that hold user data (QGPL, QUSRSYS and the like).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKDDMF/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
